        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3834630/extras/96e88aca90c6cb6029a1b20b3fc83e33.webp?t=1776611059\"><img src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3834630/extras/96e88aca90c6cb6029a1b20b3fc83e33.poster.webp?t=1776611059\" class=\"bb_img\" width=618 height=214 /></picture></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >No screaming 🤫</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dê 1 Bit ao GustavoGek</strong> is a questionable mix of <strong>horror</strong> and <strong>comedy</strong>. Just after you insult your favorite streamer, you’re dragged into a cursed game controlled by the unpredictable <strong>GlitchedGus</strong> — and now, you must <strong>collect</strong> and <strong>deliver</strong> <strong>bits</strong> to him, as he pleases. Get ready to face levels filled with challenges and bizarre enemies.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by the famous <strong>nextbots</strong> — mechanic of PNGs that chase you non-stop — the game takes this concept to the extreme with <strong>plot twists</strong>, many <strong>hidden secrets</strong>, and a <strong>sus</strong> sense of humor, all wrapped in a chaotic environment.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The main mechanic of the game is to find hidden bits and take them to the altar. However, with each level, the enemy <strong>changes</strong> its behavior, new <strong>abilities</strong> are added, and <strong>henchmen</strong> are introduced, constantly increasing the <strong>DIFFICULTY </strong>— much to the horror of casual players.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can laugh, you can shit yourself, you can laugh until you shit yourself... but don’t forget to give 1 bit.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>WARNING: THIS GAME CONTAINS FLASHING LIGHTS AND IMAGES</strong></i></p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3834630/extras/96e88aca90c6cb6029a1b20b3fc83e33.webp?t=1776611059\"><img src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3834630/extras/96e88aca90c6cb6029a1b20b3fc83e33.poster.webp?t=1776611059\" class=\"bb_img\" width=618 height=214 /></picture></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >No screaming 🤫</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dê 1 Bit ao GustavoGek</strong> is a questionable mix of <strong>horror</strong> and <strong>comedy</strong>. Just after you insult your favorite streamer, you’re dragged into a cursed game controlled by the unpredictable <strong>GlitchedGus</strong> — and now, you must <strong>collect</strong> and <strong>deliver</strong> <strong>bits</strong> to him, as he pleases. Get ready to face levels filled with challenges and bizarre enemies.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by the famous <strong>nextbots</strong> — mechanic of PNGs that chase you non-stop — the game takes this concept to the extreme with <strong>plot twists</strong>, many <strong>hidden secrets</strong>, and a <strong>sus</strong> sense of humor, all wrapped in a chaotic environment.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The main mechanic of the game is to find hidden bits and take them to the altar. However, with each level, the enemy <strong>changes</strong> its behavior, new <strong>abilities</strong> are added, and <strong>henchmen</strong> are introduced, constantly increasing the <strong>DIFFICULTY </strong>— much to the horror of casual players.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can laugh, you can shit yourself, you can laugh until you shit yourself... but don’t forget to give 1 bit.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>WARNING: THIS GAME CONTAINS FLASHING LIGHTS AND IMAGES</strong></i></p>",
        "short_description": "You've been sucked into a horror game with a single goal: deliver bits to a sus streamer. As you get closer to the exit, the challenges intensify — after all, he doesn't want the donations to ever end.",
